        With the explanations given above about the wisdom which know the mind and matter of the death moment 
        of the previous existence, one might come into the idea that only the wisdom which comprehend the nāma 
        and rūpa at the cuti moment of the immediately previous life is considered as the pubbenivāsānussati ñāṇa. 
        The above explanation is just an example. All the aggregates in the past, starting from the moment of cuti 
        18 
        in the immediate previous life, and all phenomena connected to those aggregates, are called “pubbenivāsa”, 
        and the wisdom with which one recollects them is called the “pubbenivāsānussati ñāṇa.” 35 
